<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Bugesera</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 CE – 1795 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small kingdom between Rwanda and Burundi whose lands were divided between its two powerful neighbours in the late 18th century.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Bugesera lay in the lake-strewn lowlands around Lakes Cyohoha and Rweru, on today's border between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-rwanda">Rwanda</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-burundi">Burundi</a>. Its royal clan, the Bahondogo, are remembered in Rwandan and Burundian traditions as rulers of one of the older kingdoms of the region, dating to at least the 16th century.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is known of its government beyond royal rituals and drums similar to those of its neighbours. It was a land of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> and farming, and its rulers engaged in alliances and wars with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-rwanda">Kingdom of Rwanda</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-burundi">Kingdom of Burundi</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Bugesera was conquered and partitioned around the end of the 18th century, with the northern part absorbed by <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-rwanda">Rwanda</a> and the southern by <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-burundi">Burundi</a>. Bugesera survives as a district name in Rwanda.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-bugesera.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Bugesera" width="320" height="277"><figcaption>Image: Applodion · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kingdom_of_Bugesera.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1500 CE – 1795 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Kirundi, Kinyarwanda</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/rwanda">Rwanda</a>, <a href="/countries/burundi">Burundi</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Bugesera</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1648&amp;focus=kingdom-of-bugesera" aria-label="Kingdom of Bugesera on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5516 2249 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Bugesera lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5826 2522h0M5827 2571h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5836 2505h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5836 2505h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Rwanda. <a href="/atlas?year=1648&amp;focus=kingdom-of-bugesera">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

